 "posture": "Equity risk appetite rebounded sharply — S&P 500 +1.3% to 7,619 and Nasdaq-100 +2.3% — as CoreWeave's blowout quarter and a reportedly oversubscribed Anthropic IPO revived AI-infrastructure confidence, with the VIX easing 10% to 17.5 (normal 16–20 band). Breadth is the catch: the TraderMonty composite reads 49.4/100 in the Neutral zone (60–75% equity band), the 200-day breadth trend is still falling, and only 24 of the collector's 75 universe names sit above their 50-day average — a narrow, selective rally. The macro backdrop stays restrictive: after hot October CPI, markets price ~87% odds of a December hike and the 10Y sits at 5.00%, keeping pressure on duration-sensitive risk. Crypto reads 53.2/100 Neutral — BTC in a bull pullback between its 50- and 200-day averages, ~26% below its 1-year high, funding warming to ~18% annualized, but only 10% of the top-20 positive over 30 days. Net: participate selectively inside the 60–75% equity band, favor cash-flow-backed AI winners over story names, and keep rate-sensitive exposure light ahead of tomorrow's PPI.",
 "sentiment": "Constructive but fragile: the AI-infrastructure complex is where risk appetite is being expressed, yet hot inflation, a 5.00% 10-year and persistent crypto ETF outflows suggest this is a rebound within a corrective regime rather than a wholesale risk-on turn.",
